  "findings": [
    "Pinned go-quai applies the cubic conversion discount to the total of all conversions in a prime batch, processed in descending slippage order. Single-transaction quote RPCs (quai_quaiToQi, quai_calculateConversionAmount) cannot predict it.",
    "A recurring third-party Qi->Quai conversion (~255-280 QUAI, 1500 bps slippage) shared all three batches. Observed batch discounts of about 2.8-12.8% reverted 100 and 500 bps conversions and reduced a successful one by 2.8%.",
    "The SDK credit observer correctly classified both reverts as RefundReported and the successful settlement as ConversionReported with exact outputs and locks.",
    "Harness stage-chaining in zsh ignored failures because PIPESTATUS is bash-only; no unsigned payload was ever broadcast. Stages now run through bash with pipefail.",
    "Size/slippage policy chosen from the pinned discount formula: 200 QUAI at 800 bps accepted single-competitor batches (~5.4%) and refunded a two-competitor batch for only the origin fee.",
    "Mainnet origin inclusion can exceed the harness's 90 s receipt wait; retrying observation of the same saved hash reconciled it without rebroadcast."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Trusted public gateway observations, not independent consensus proofs.",
    "No Qi spend is possible until the conversion locks expire at blocks 10338942, 10339066 and 10339111.",
    "Third-party batch flow is an observation of this period, not a stable rate."
  ],
